"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_hj5m0hwcsji9uu1ac2q327fp","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nmodel: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813\ntools: read,grep,glob,bash\nthinking: high\n---\n# Verifier\n\nReview one exact Canopy Revision and publish durable Checks and Verdict evidence.\nCanopy is a read-only view over external Forests through `forest.cli.v2`; do\nnot import Iron Forest, inspect `.forest`, open its Ledger, or repair code.\n\n## Select one Revision\n\n1. Run `git fetch origin` and\n   `git ls-remote origin 'refs/heads/forest/*' 'refs/forest/v1/*'`.\n2. Select one branch tip with request evidence and no verdict evidence. Fetch\n   the request ref, require its committer to be\n   `Iron Forest Builder <builder@forest.invalid>` or\n   `Iron Forest Fixer <fixer@forest.invalid>`, and require `request.json` to\n   name that branch and exact tip SHA.\n3. Check out that exact SHA in the provided worktree. Do not review a moving\n   branch or create a nested worktree.\n\n## Gate and review\n\n1. Read `forest.yaml` from the Revision and run every `checks:` command in\n   listed order, recording each name and numeric exit code.\n2. Review the diff from the current primary ref through the exact SHA. Trace\n   changed paths, callers, errors, state, cleanup, trust boundaries, and\n   available actionable review feedback. Report only evidence-backed findings;\n   each `changes` reason names the wrong state, required state, and evidence.\n3. Before approval, require the exact SHA to contain the current primary ref:\n   `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/} <sha>`.\n   A stale SHA receives `changes` and never enters the approval Gate.\n4. Approve only when all checks pass, ancestry holds, and no blocking finding\n   remains. Write these exact payloads outside the repository:\n\n   ```json\n   {\"schema\":\"forest.checks.v1\",\"revision\":\"<full-sha>\",\"results\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"ok\":true,\"exit\":0}],\"time\":\"<rfc3339>\"}\n   {\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"<full-sha>\",\"verdict\":\"approve|changes\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"time\":\"<rfc3339>\"}\n   ```\n\n## Publish\n\nAfter both payloads exist, call only:\n\n```sh\nforest publish verdict \"$checks_payload_file\" \"$verdict_payload_file\"\n```\n\nThe Kernel validates evidence, performs configured Checks, and atomically\nfast-forwards `master` on approval. Do not use raw `git push`, force flags, or\npublish a different SHA. Powder completion is Kernel-owned; do not call Powder\nfrom this declaration. Report no-work, malformed evidence, failed checks,\nstale revisions, rejected merges, credential exposure, and other unexpected\nstate with exact evidence.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550635942},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This matches the system prompt. Now let me decide selection. There might be an ordering hint in `forest poll verifier`. Let me check that trigger.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"This matches the system prompt. Now let me decide selection. There might be an ordering hint in `forest poll verifier`. Let me check that trigger.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_uethgiqfmv0y1kihn0a7l2pc","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy && ./forest trigger show verifier --json 2>&1; echo \"---POLL---\"; ./forest poll verifier --json 2>&1 | head -60"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813","usage":{"input":1335,"output":124,"cacheRead":19456,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":31,"totalTokens":20915,"cost":{"input":0.0008811,"output":0.00024552,"cacheRead":0.00042803199999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0015546520000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788550635943,"responseId":"gen-1788550636-DHBTYQsvKOGIXVc7I8E4","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCall